IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpq13a-dates`
IMPORT `cpq13a-member`

-- Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland), Part 13A -- worked cases for the questions of a person with a claim in a
-- representative proceeding (cpq13a-member.l4) and the date helpers (cpq13a-dates.l4). Every expected value was worked
-- by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the
-- ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts and dates are illustrative.
-- Day counts used: 6 months after 31 August 2026 is 28 February 2027 (2027 has no 29 February: fork F9); 6 months after
-- 31 August 2027 is 29 February 2028; 6 months after 15 March 2027 is 15 September 2027; the day before 1 March 2028 is
-- 29 February 2028; from 1 June 2027 to 30 June 2027 is 29 days, so a period suspended on 1 June 2027 with 30 June 2027
-- as its last day has 29 days left: running again on 10 August 2027 it ends 8 September 2027 (10 August + 21 = 31
-- August, + 8 = 8 September), and running again on 1 February 2029 it ends 2 March 2029 (February 2029 has 28 days);
-- 21 days after 29 March 2027 is 19 April 2027.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `the date helpers`
-- ===================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `the date` 6 `months after` (`d` 31 8 2026) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `the date` 6 `months after` (`d` 31 8 2027) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `the date` 6 `months after` (`d` 15 3 2027) EQUALS `d` 15 9 2027
#ASSERT `the date` 6 `months after` (`d` 15 9 2027) EQUALS `d` 15 3 2028
#ASSERT `the day before` (`d` 1 3 2028) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `the day` 21 `days after` (`d` 29 3 2027) EQUALS `d` 19 4 2027
#ASSERT `the days from` (`d` 1 6 2027) `to` (`d` 30 6 2027) EQUALS 29

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 103B, 103C, 103F, 111 -- starting a representative proceeding`
-- ===================================================================================================================

`can start` MEANS `yes: 7 or more persons have claims against the same person, arising out of the same, similar or related circumstances and giving rise to a substantial common issue of law or fact (s 103B(1)); 1 or more of them may start it for some or all of the others (s 103B(2))`
`before Part 13A` MEANS `no: Part 13A applies only to a proceeding started after it commenced (s 111(1))`
`under 7` MEANS `no: fewer than 7 persons have claims against the same person (s 103B(1)(a))`
`unrelated` MEANS `no: the claims do not all arise out of the same, similar or related circumstances (s 103B(1)(b))`
`no common issue` MEANS `no: the claims do not all give rise to a substantial common issue of law or fact (s 103B(1)(c))`

-- 7 persons is enough; 6 is not (the threshold, s 103B(1)(a)).
#ASSERT `Can a representative proceeding be started for my claim` TRUE 7 TRUE TRUE EQUALS `can start`
#ASSERT `Can a representative proceeding be started for my claim` TRUE 6 TRUE TRUE EQUALS `under 7`
#ASSERT `Can a representative proceeding be started for my claim` TRUE 1000 TRUE TRUE EQUALS `can start`
#ASSERT `Can a representative proceeding be started for my claim` TRUE 7 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `unrelated`
#ASSERT `Can a representative proceeding be started for my claim` TRUE 7 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no common issue`
#ASSERT `Can a representative proceeding be started for my claim` FALSE 1000 TRUE TRUE EQUALS `before Part 13A`
#ASSERT `Can a representative proceeding be started for my claim` TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `under 7`

`I can start it` MEANS `yes: you may start it, as the representative party, on behalf of the others (ss 103B(2), 103C(1)); against more than 1 defendant if you wish, even if not every group member has a claim against each (s 103C(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I start a representative proceeding` TRUE 7 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `I can start it`
#ASSERT `Can I start a representative proceeding` TRUE 6 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: a representative proceeding cannot be started for these claims (s 103B(1) or s 111)`
#ASSERT `Can I start a representative proceeding` FALSE 50 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: a representative proceeding cannot be started for these claims (s 103B(1) or s 111)`
#ASSERT `Can I start a representative proceeding` TRUE 50 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: you need a claim of your own against the proposed defendant, as one of the 7 or more (s 103C(1))`
#ASSERT `Can I start a representative proceeding` TRUE 50 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: you need standing to start a proceeding on your own behalf against the proposed defendant (s 103C(1))`

-- s 103C(3): the person who started it keeps standing after their claim ends; a substituted representative: silent.
#ASSERT `Can I carry on after my own claim ends` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I carry on after my own claim ends` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I carry on after my own claim ends` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I carry on after my own claim ends` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 103F: all three limbs needed.
#ASSERT `Does my originating process meet s 103F` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my originating process meet s 103F` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my originating process meet s 103F` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my originating process meet s 103F` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 103A, 103D, 103E -- being a group member`
-- ===================================================================================================================

`private` MEANS `a private person, company or other body`
`member, no consent needed` MEANS `yes: you are within the description of the group, and your consent is not needed (s 103D(1))`
`member by consent` MEANS `yes: you are within the description of the group and have consented in writing (s 103D(2))`
`not described` MEANS `no: you are not within the description of the group members in the originating process (s 103A, s 103F(1)(a))`
`government without consent` MEANS `no: as the Commonwealth, a State, a Minister, a public body or an officer, you are a group member only if you consent in writing (s 103D(2))`
`opted out of the group` MEANS `no: you have opted out (s 103G)`

#ASSERT `Am I a group member` TRUE `private` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `member, no consent needed`
#ASSERT `Am I a group member` TRUE `private` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `member, no consent needed`
#ASSERT `Am I a group member` TRUE `the Commonwealth or a State` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `government without consent`
#ASSERT `Am I a group member` TRUE `a Minister of the Commonwealth or a State` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `member by consent`
#ASSERT `Am I a group member` TRUE `a body corporate established for a public purpose by a law of the Commonwealth or a State (not an incorporated company or association)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `government without consent`
#ASSERT `Am I a group member` TRUE `an officer of the Commonwealth or a State, acting in that capacity` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `opted out of the group`
#ASSERT `Am I a group member` TRUE `private` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `opted out of the group`
#ASSERT `Am I a group member` FALSE `private` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not described`
#ASSERT `Am I a group member` FALSE `the Commonwealth or a State` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not described`

#ASSERT `Do I need a litigation guardian` TRUE `just be a group member` EQUALS `no: a person under a legal incapacity does not need a litigation guardian merely to be a group member (s 103E(1))`
#ASSERT `Do I need a litigation guardian` TRUE `take a step in the proceeding or conduct part of it` EQUALS `yes: as a group member under a legal incapacity you may take a step or conduct part of the proceeding only by your litigation guardian (s 103E(2))`
#ASSERT `Do I need a litigation guardian` FALSE `take a step in the proceeding or conduct part of it` EQUALS `not covered: s 103E is only about persons under a legal incapacity`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 103G -- opting out`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- A proceeding started 1 March 2027; the court fixes 1 June 2027 as the date before which members may opt out.
`opted out in time` MEANS `yes: you opted out by written notice before the date the court fixed (s 103G(2))`
`no notice` MEANS `no: you have not given written notice of opting out (s 103G(2))`
`notice too late` MEANS `no: your notice was given on or after the date the court fixed for opting out (s 103G(2)); the court may fix a later date on an application (s 103G(3))`
`notice too early` MEANS `not covered: your notice was given before the representative proceeding started`
`unused` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000

-- The last day is 31 May 2027 (the day before the date); 1 June 2027 is too late.
#ASSERT `Have I opted out in time` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) FALSE `unused` TRUE (`d` 31 5 2027) EQUALS `opted out in time`
#ASSERT `Have I opted out in time` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) FALSE `unused` TRUE (`d` 1 6 2027) EQUALS `notice too late`
#ASSERT `Have I opted out in time` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) FALSE `unused` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `opted out in time`
#ASSERT `Have I opted out in time` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) FALSE `unused` TRUE (`d` 28 2 2027) EQUALS `notice too early`
#ASSERT `Have I opted out in time` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) FALSE `unused` FALSE (`d` 31 5 2027) EQUALS `no notice`
-- A later date, 1 July 2027 (s 103G(3)): 30 June is in time, 1 July is not; 15 June is in time though after the first date.
#ASSERT `Have I opted out in time` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) TRUE (`d` 1 7 2027) TRUE (`d` 30 6 2027) EQUALS `opted out in time`
#ASSERT `Have I opted out in time` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) TRUE (`d` 1 7 2027) TRUE (`d` 15 6 2027) EQUALS `opted out in time`
#ASSERT `Have I opted out in time` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) TRUE (`d` 1 7 2027) TRUE (`d` 1 7 2027) EQUALS `notice too late`

#ASSERT `What is the last day I can opt out` (`d` 1 6 2027) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `d` 31 5 2027
#ASSERT `What is the last day I can opt out` (`d` 1 6 2027) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2028) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2028

-- s 103G(4): a hearing the day before the date needs leave; on the date it does not.
#ASSERT `Can the hearing start before the opt-out date` (`d` 1 6 2027) (`d` 31 5 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the hearing start before the opt-out date` (`d` 1 6 2027) (`d` 31 5 2027) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the hearing start before the opt-out date` (`d` 1 6 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 103H -- joining the group when your cause of action accrued later`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- Started 1 March 2027; leave given fixing 1 June 2027.
`added` MEANS `yes: the court has given leave, and the description of the group may be changed to include you (s 103H(1), (2))`
`may be added` MEANS `possibly: you qualify under s 103H(2); the representative party may apply for leave to change the description of the group to include you, and the court decides`
`accrued too early` MEANS `not covered by s 103H: your cause of action did not accrue after the proceeding started (you may already be within the description of the group)`
`accrued too late` MEANS `not covered by s 103H: your cause of action accrued on or after the date the court fixed when giving leave (s 103H(2)(a))`
`never a member` MEANS `not covered by s 103H: you would not have been a group member even if your cause of action had accrued before the proceeding started (s 103H(2)(b))`

#ASSERT `Can I be added to the group after my cause accrued` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 5 2027) TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 6 2027) EQUALS `added`
#ASSERT `Can I be added to the group after my cause accrued` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 31 5 2027) TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 6 2027) EQUALS `added`
#ASSERT `Can I be added to the group after my cause accrued` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 6 2027) EQUALS `accrued too late`
#ASSERT `Can I be added to the group after my cause accrued` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 2 3 2027) TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 6 2027) EQUALS `added`
#ASSERT `Can I be added to the group after my cause accrued` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 6 2027) EQUALS `accrued too early`
#ASSERT `Can I be added to the group after my cause accrued` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 5 2027) TRUE FALSE `unused` EQUALS `may be added`
#ASSERT `Can I be added to the group after my cause accrued` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 5 2027) FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 6 2027) EQUALS `never a member`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 103Z -- the limitation period`
-- ===================================================================================================================

`suspended` MEANS `yes: the limitation period for your claim stopped running when the representative proceeding started, and has not started again (s 103Z(1), (2))`
`running after opt out` MEANS `no, it is running again: you opted out (s 103Z(2)(a))`
`running after decision` MEANS `no, it is running again: the proceeding and any appeal were decided without finally disposing of your claim (s 103Z(2)(b))`
`disposed` MEANS `not needed: your claim has been finally disposed of in the representative proceeding`
`gap` MEANS `not covered: s 103Z(2) does not say whether the period runs again after an order that the proceeding no longer continue under Part 13A, or after an approved settlement or discontinuance`
`not a member` MEANS `not covered: s 103Z applies to the claim of a group member to which the proceeding relates`

`going` MEANS `it is still going`
`opted` MEANS `I opted out under s 103G`
`decided open` MEANS `it and any appeal were decided without finally disposing of my claim`
`decided closed` MEANS `it and any appeal were decided, finally disposing of my claim`
`declassed` MEANS `the court ordered that it no longer continue under Part 13A`
`settled` MEANS `it was settled or discontinued with the court's approval`

#ASSERT `Is my limitation period suspended` TRUE `going` EQUALS `suspended`
#ASSERT `Is my limitation period suspended` TRUE `opted` EQUALS `running after opt out`
#ASSERT `Is my limitation period suspended` TRUE `decided open` EQUALS `running after decision`
#ASSERT `Is my limitation period suspended` TRUE `decided closed` EQUALS `disposed`
#ASSERT `Is my limitation period suspended` TRUE `declassed` EQUALS `gap`
#ASSERT `Is my limitation period suspended` TRUE `settled` EQUALS `gap`
#ASSERT `Is my limitation period suspended` FALSE `going` EQUALS `not a member`

-- Last day 30 June 2027, proceeding started 1 June 2027: 29 days left.
#ASSERT `By when must I start my own proceeding` (`d` 30 6 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) TRUE `opted` (`d` 10 8 2027) EQUALS JUST (`d` 8 9 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must I start my own proceeding` (`d` 30 6 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) TRUE `decided open` (`d` 1 2 2029) EQUALS JUST (`d` 2 3 2029)
-- The period's last day was the day the proceeding started: no days left, it ends the day it runs again (fork F8).
#ASSERT `By when must I start my own proceeding` (`d` 1 6 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) TRUE `opted` (`d` 10 8 2027) EQUALS JUST (`d` 10 8 2027)
-- The period had already ended before the proceeding started: nothing to suspend.
#ASSERT `By when must I start my own proceeding` (`d` 31 5 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) TRUE `opted` (`d` 10 8 2027) EQUALS JUST (`d` 31 5 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must I start my own proceeding` (`d` 30 6 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) TRUE `going` `unused` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `By when must I start my own proceeding` (`d` 30 6 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) TRUE `declassed` (`d` 10 8 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `By when must I start my own proceeding` (`d` 30 6 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) TRUE `decided closed` (`d` 10 8 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `By when must I start my own proceeding` (`d` 30 6 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) FALSE `opted` (`d` 10 8 2027) EQUALS NOTHING

`in time on my own` MEANS `yes: you start within the limitation period, counting the suspension under s 103Z`
`out of time on my own` MEANS `no: the limitation period has run out, even counting the suspension under s 103Z`

-- The last day, 8 September 2027, and the day after.
#ASSERT `Am I in time to start my own proceeding` (`d` 30 6 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) TRUE `opted` (`d` 10 8 2027) (`d` 8 9 2027) EQUALS `in time on my own`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to start my own proceeding` (`d` 30 6 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) TRUE `opted` (`d` 10 8 2027) (`d` 9 9 2027) EQUALS `out of time on my own`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to start my own proceeding` (`d` 30 6 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) TRUE `opted` (`d` 10 8 2027) (`d` 10 8 2027) EQUALS `in time on my own`
-- Starting during the suspension, after the old last day.
#ASSERT `Am I in time to start my own proceeding` (`d` 30 6 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) TRUE `opted` (`d` 10 8 2027) (`d` 15 7 2027) EQUALS `in time on my own`
-- 2 March 2029 and 3 March 2029, after a decision on 1 February 2029.
#ASSERT `Am I in time to start my own proceeding` (`d` 30 6 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) TRUE `decided open` (`d` 1 2 2029) (`d` 2 3 2029) EQUALS `in time on my own`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to start my own proceeding` (`d` 30 6 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) TRUE `decided open` (`d` 1 2 2029) (`d` 3 3 2029) EQUALS `out of time on my own`
-- The period ended (31 May 2027) before the proceeding started (1 June 2027).
#ASSERT `Am I in time to start my own proceeding` (`d` 31 5 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) TRUE `opted` (`d` 10 8 2027) (`d` 20 5 2027) EQUALS `in time on my own`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to start my own proceeding` (`d` 31 5 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) TRUE `opted` (`d` 10 8 2027) (`d` 1 7 2027) EQUALS `out of time on my own`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to start my own proceeding` (`d` 31 5 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) TRUE `opted` (`d` 10 8 2027) (`d` 10 8 2027) EQUALS `out of time on my own`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to start my own proceeding` (`d` 30 6 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) TRUE `going` `unused` (`d` 1 1 2030) EQUALS `no need to count: the limitation period is still suspended (s 103Z(1), (2))`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to start my own proceeding` (`d` 30 6 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) TRUE `decided closed` (`d` 10 8 2027) (`d` 1 9 2027) EQUALS `not covered: s 103Z does not decide this (ask whether your limitation period is suspended)`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to start my own proceeding` (`d` 30 6 2027) (`d` 1 6 2027) FALSE `going` `unused` (`d` 1 9 2027) EQUALS `not covered: s 103Z does not decide this (ask whether your limitation period is suspended)`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 103V, 103W, 103X, 103ZC -- judgment, damages and the fund`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 103X with s 103U(8): not receiving a notice makes no difference.
#ASSERT `Am I bound by the judgment` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I bound by the judgment` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I bound by the judgment` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I bound by the judgment` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I bound by the judgment` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `Can damages be awarded as one total` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes, the court may award damages in an aggregate amount: a reasonably accurate assessment of the total can be made (s 103V(1)(f), (3))`
#ASSERT `Can damages be awarded as one total` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the court must not award damages in an aggregate amount unless a reasonably accurate assessment of the total can be made (s 103V(3))`
#ASSERT `Can damages be awarded as one total` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes, the court may: the aggregate amount comes with a settlement approved under s 103R, to which s 103V(3) does not apply`

-- s 103W(3)(c): exactly 6 months on is enough; a day less is not.
#ASSERT `Does the fund claim date meet s 103W` (`d` 31 8 2026) (`d` 28 2 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the fund claim date meet s 103W` (`d` 31 8 2026) (`d` 27 2 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the fund claim date meet s 103W` (`d` 15 3 2027) (`d` 15 9 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the fund claim date meet s 103W` (`d` 15 3 2027) (`d` 14 9 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the fund claim date meet s 103W` (`d` 15 3 2027) (`d` 1 1 2028) EQUALS JUST TRUE

`fund in time` MEANS `yes: you claim before the date stated in the order (s 103W(3)(c))`
`fund late, allowed` MEANS `yes, late: the court has allowed you to claim after the date, the fund not being fully distributed (s 103W(4))`
`fund late, may be allowed` MEANS `late: the court may allow a late claim if it considers it just, while the fund is not fully distributed (s 103W(4)); it has not yet done so`
`fund late, gone` MEANS `no: your claim is late and the fund has been fully distributed (s 103W(4))`

-- Order 15 March 2027, claims before 15 September 2027: the last day is 14 September 2027.
#ASSERT `Am I in time to claim from the fund` (`d` 15 3 2027) (`d` 15 9 2027) (`d` 14 9 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `fund in time`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to claim from the fund` (`d` 15 3 2027) (`d` 15 9 2027) (`d` 15 3 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `fund in time`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to claim from the fund` (`d` 15 3 2027) (`d` 15 9 2027) (`d` 14 9 2027) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `fund in time`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to claim from the fund` (`d` 15 3 2027) (`d` 15 9 2027) (`d` 15 9 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `fund late, may be allowed`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to claim from the fund` (`d` 15 3 2027) (`d` 15 9 2027) (`d` 15 9 2027) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `fund late, allowed`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to claim from the fund` (`d` 15 3 2027) (`d` 15 9 2027) (`d` 1 2 2028) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `fund late, gone`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to claim from the fund` (`d` 15 3 2027) (`d` 15 9 2027) (`d` 1 2 2028) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `fund late, gone`

-- s 103ZC: the whole excess at most; nothing if no award, no application, or no excess.
#ASSERT `What is the most paid out of the damages for the representative party's costs` TRUE TRUE 500000 350000 EQUALS 150000
#ASSERT `What is the most paid out of the damages for the representative party's costs` TRUE TRUE 350001 350000 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `What is the most paid out of the damages for the representative party's costs` TRUE TRUE 350000 350000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What is the most paid out of the damages for the representative party's costs` TRUE TRUE 300000 350000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What is the most paid out of the damages for the representative party's costs` FALSE TRUE 500000 350000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What is the most paid out of the damages for the representative party's costs` TRUE FALSE 500000 350000 EQUALS 0

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 103M, 103N, 103ZB -- costs`
-- ===================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay costs` `the representative party` FALSE EQUALS `yes: as the representative party you are a party, and the court may order you to pay costs (s 103ZB(a))`
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay costs` `the representative party` TRUE EQUALS `yes: as the representative party you are a party, and the court may order you to pay costs (s 103ZB(a))`
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay costs` `a sub-group representative party appointed under s 103M` FALSE EQUALS `yes, but only the costs of deciding the issues common to your sub-group, for which you, not the representative party, are liable (ss 103M(3), 103ZB(b))`
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay costs` `a sub-group representative party appointed under s 103M` TRUE EQUALS `yes, but only the costs of deciding the issues common to your sub-group and of the issue that relates only to your claim (ss 103M(3), 103N(2), 103ZB(b))`
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay costs` `a group member who is neither` TRUE EQUALS `yes, but only the costs of deciding the issue that relates only to your claim, for which you, not the representative party, are liable (ss 103N(2), 103ZB(b))`
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay costs` `a group member who is neither` FALSE EQUALS `no: the court may not order a group member who is not a representative party to pay costs (s 103ZB(b))`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 103T, 103U -- notices`
-- ===================================================================================================================

`must notify` MEANS `yes: notice must be given to group members as soon as practicable after the event (s 103T(1), (6))`
`dispensed` MEANS `no: the court has dispensed with the notice, as it may because the relief sought does not include damages (s 103T(2))`
`ordered` MEANS `yes: the court has ordered that notice be given, as soon as practicable after the event (s 103T(3), (5), (6))`
`only if ordered` MEANS `only if the court orders it (s 103T(3), (5))`
`start` MEANS `the start of the proceeding and my right to opt out`

-- s 103T(2): a dispensation counts only where no damages are claimed.
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice` `start` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `must notify`
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice` `start` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `must notify`
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice` `start` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `dispensed`
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice` `start` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `must notify`
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice` `the defendant's application to dismiss the proceeding for want of prosecution` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `must notify`
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice` `the representative party's application for leave to withdraw` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `dispensed`
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice` `a payment into court of money in answer to a cause of action in the proceeding` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `only if ordered`
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice` `a payment into court of money in answer to a cause of action in the proceeding` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ordered`
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice` `any other matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `only if ordered`
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice` `any other matter` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ordered`
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice` `an application to approve a settlement` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the settlement must not be decided until notice has been given to group members (s 103T(4))`
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice` `an application to approve a settlement` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: the court considers it just to decide the settlement application without notice (s 103T(4))`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 103R, 103S, 103P -- settlement, and the representative party`
-- ===================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Can the proceeding be settled or discontinued` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the proceeding be settled or discontinued` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I settle my own claim as representative party` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I settle my own claim as representative party` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `Can I withdraw as representative party` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the court has given you leave to withdraw (s 103S(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw as representative party` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `possibly: the conditions in s 103S(4) are met, and the court may give you leave to withdraw (s 103S(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw as representative party` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not yet: the court must first be satisfied that group members were told of your application in time to seek a substitute (s 103S(4)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw as representative party` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not yet: any application to substitute a group member as representative party must be decided first (s 103S(4)(b))`
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw as representative party` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not covered: s 103S(2) lets a representative party withdraw when seeking leave to settle, or having settled, their individual claim`

`may apply only` MEANS `you may apply, but the court may substitute only if it considers the representative cannot adequately represent the group or sub-group (s 103P)`
#ASSERT `Can the representative party be replaced` `the representative party` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you may apply, and the court may substitute another group member as the representative party, because it considers the representative party cannot adequately represent the group (s 103P(1))`
#ASSERT `Can the representative party be replaced` `the representative party` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: you may apply, and the court may substitute a group member as the representative party, because the representative party seeks leave to withdraw (s 103S(3))`
#ASSERT `Can the representative party be replaced` `the representative party` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `may apply only`
#ASSERT `Can the representative party be replaced` `the representative party of my sub-group` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you may apply, and the court may substitute another person as the sub-group representative party, because it considers that party cannot adequately represent the sub-group (s 103P(2))`
#ASSERT `Can the representative party be replaced` `the representative party of my sub-group` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `may apply only`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 103I, 103J, 103K, 103L, 103Q`
-- ===================================================================================================================

`103I` MEANS `yes: the court may order that it no longer continue under Part 13A (or that it continue), as it appears likely there are fewer than 7 group members (s 103I)`
`103J` MEANS `yes: the court may order that it no longer continue under Part 13A, or stay the claim for money for group members, as distribution costs would be excessive (s 103J)`
`103K` MEANS `yes: the court may order that it no longer continue under Part 13A, in the interests of justice (s 103K(1))`
`stays representative` MEANS `no: none of ss 103I, 103J and 103K applies on these facts`

#ASSERT `Can the proceeding stop being a representative proceeding` TRUE FALSE FALSE `none` EQUALS `103I`
#ASSERT `Can the proceeding stop being a representative proceeding` FALSE TRUE TRUE `none` EQUALS `103J`
#ASSERT `Can the proceeding stop being a representative proceeding` FALSE FALSE TRUE `none` EQUALS `stays representative`
#ASSERT `Can the proceeding stop being a representative proceeding` FALSE TRUE FALSE `none` EQUALS `stays representative`
#ASSERT `Can the proceeding stop being a representative proceeding` FALSE FALSE FALSE `not an efficient and effective way of dealing with the claims` EQUALS `103K`
#ASSERT `Can the proceeding stop being a representative proceeding` FALSE FALSE FALSE `the representative party cannot adequately represent the group members` EQUALS `103K`
#ASSERT `Can the proceeding stop being a representative proceeding` FALSE FALSE FALSE `otherwise inappropriate, for a reason beyond the group's make-up or a funding arrangement` EQUALS `103K`
-- s 103K(2): a funding arrangement or a partial group is not, by itself, enough.
#ASSERT `Can the proceeding stop being a representative proceeding` FALSE FALSE FALSE `otherwise inappropriate, merely because the group leaves out others or is aggregated for a funding arrangement` EQUALS `stays representative`

#ASSERT `What can I do after the proceeding stops being representative` TRUE `I am the representative party` EQUALS `you may continue the proceeding on your own behalf against the defendant (s 103L(a))`
#ASSERT `What can I do after the proceeding stops being representative` TRUE `I am a group member` EQUALS `you may apply to be joined as a plaintiff in the continued proceeding, and the court may order it (s 103L(b))`
#ASSERT `What can I do after the proceeding stops being representative` FALSE `I am a group member` EQUALS `not covered: s 103L applies after an order under s 103I, 103J or 103K that the proceeding no longer continue under Part 13A`

#ASSERT `Can my relief be held back` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my relief be held back` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 103Y -- appeals`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- Judgment 1 March 2027; the representative party's time ends 29 March 2027 (an illustrative 28 days); the further 21
-- days end 19 April 2027.
`appeal in time` MEANS `yes: the representative party did not appeal in time, and you start an appeal on behalf of the group within the further 21 days (s 103Y(3))`
`appeal too late` MEANS `no: the further 21 days for a group member's appeal have passed (s 103Y(3))`
`appeal not yet` MEANS `not yet: s 103Y(3) gives a group member a right to appeal once the representative party's time for appealing has passed without an appeal`

#ASSERT `Can I appeal on behalf of the group` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 29 3 2027) (`d` 19 4 2027) EQUALS `appeal in time`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal on behalf of the group` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 29 3 2027) (`d` 20 4 2027) EQUALS `appeal too late`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal on behalf of the group` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 29 3 2027) (`d` 30 3 2027) EQUALS `appeal in time`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal on behalf of the group` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 29 3 2027) (`d` 29 3 2027) EQUALS `appeal not yet`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal on behalf of the group` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 29 3 2027) (`d` 10 4 2027) EQUALS `no need: the representative party has started an appeal, as representative of the group (s 103Y(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal on behalf of the group` FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 29 3 2027) (`d` 10 4 2027) EQUALS `not covered: s 103Y(3) lets a member of the group or sub-group appeal`

#ASSERT `By when must I appeal on behalf of the group` FALSE (`d` 29 3 2027) EQUALS JUST (`d` 19 4 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must I appeal on behalf of the group` FALSE (`d` 20 12 2027) EQUALS JUST (`d` 10 1 2028)
#ASSERT `By when must I appeal on behalf of the group` TRUE (`d` 29 3 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
